    {
      "id": "question_1",
      "provider": "question",
      "name": "Question",
      "config": {
        "type": "question"
      },
      "input": [
        {
          "lane": "text",
          "from": "dispute_in"
        }
      ],
      "ui": {
        "position": {
          "x": 240,
          "y": 200
        },
        "measured": {
          "width": 150,
          "height": 66
        },
        "nodeType": "default",
        "formDataValid": true
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "letter_prompt",
      "provider": "prompt",
      "name": "Prompt",
      "config": {
        "instructions": [
          "You are a chargeback dispute analyst writing to a card payment processor's dispute-resolution team.",
          "",
          "The user message is a JSON object describing ONE dispute. It already contains every fact you may use:",
          "- dispute_id, reason_code, amount, currency",
          "- confidence_score (0-100) and confidence_label, already computed by the merchant's system",
          "- signals: delivery_confirmed, delivery_photo_available, device_match, address_match, prior_disputes_count, days_since_delivery",
          "- order, session, delivery, customer: the raw records looked up from the merchant's systems (fields may be null when a lookup failed)",
          "- missing_evidence: a list of evidence items that could NOT be gathered",
          "",
          "Write a firm, professional evidence letter (150-300 words) that:",
          "1. Opens by identifying the dispute_id and the reason_code being contested.",
          "2. Cites the SPECIFIC favorable signals present (e.g. 'delivery was confirmed by <carrier> on <delivered_at>', 'the order device fingerprint matched the customer's profile', 'the billing and shipping addresses match', 'this customer has no prior disputes'). Only mention a signal if it is actually true/favorable in the input.",
          "3. If missing_evidence is non-empty, briefly acknowledges the gaps and states that the remaining record still supports the charge (or, when confidence_label is 'weak evidence' or 'insufficient evidence', requests a manual review instead of asserting a win).",
          "4. Tailors the argument to reason_code: 'product_not_received' -> lead with delivery proof; 'unauthorized_transaction' -> lead with device/IP/address match and account history; 'duplicate_charge' -> note that this is a single distinct transaction and no duplicate settlement was found.",
          "5. Closes by requesting the dispute be resolved in the merchant's favor.",
          "",
          "Do NOT invent facts, tracking numbers, dates, or amounts that are not in the input. Do NOT use markdown or backticks.",
          "",
          "Return ONLY a JSON object with exactly these two keys:",
          "{\"evidence_letter\": \"<the full letter as one string>\", \"confidence_explanation\": \"<one sentence explaining why the confidence score is what it is>\"}"
        ],
        "parameters": {}
      },
      "input": [
        {
          "lane": "questions",
          "from": "question_1"
        }
      ],
      "ui": {
        "position": {
          "x": 460,
          "y": 200
        },
        "measured": {
          "width": 150,
          "height": 86
        },
        "nodeType": "default",
        "formDataValid": true
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "letter_llm",
      "provider": "llm_ollama",
      "name": "Ollama",
      "config": {
        "profile": "llama3_2-3b",
        "llama3_2-3b": {
          "model": "llama3.2",
          "serverbase": "http://127.0.0.1:11434/v1"
        },
        "parameters": {}
      },
      "input": [
        {
          "lane": "questions",
          "from": "letter_prompt"
        }
      ],
      "ui": {
        "position": {
          "x": 680,
          "y": 200
        },
        "measured": {
          "width": 150,
          "height": 66
        },
        "nodeType": "default",
        "formDataValid": true
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "letter_out",
      "provider": "response_answers",
      "name": "Return Answers",
      "config": {
        "laneName": "answers"
      },
      "input": [
        {
          "lane": "answers",
          "from": "letter_llm"
        }
      ],
      "ui": {
        "position": {
          "x": 900,
          "y": 200
        },
        "measured": {
          "width": 150,
          "height": 66
        },
        "nodeType": "default",
        "formDataValid": true
      }
    }
  ],
